WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.928
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for silent e and long vowels.

2
00:00:04.378 --> 00:00:06.338
Here is a word your child can read.

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:10.456
The word is cap.

4
00:00:11.356 --> 00:00:13.267
Now one letter is added at the end.

5
00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.692
A child who is stuck here reads the same word again, or stops.

6
00:00:18.292 --> 00:00:22.413
The goal of this plan is a child who looks at the end first. Like this.

7
00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:26.631
The word is cape.

8
00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:33.219
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

9
00:00:34.019 --> 00:00:38.263
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

10
00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:43.726
This plan is for a child who reads short words, but gets stuck on longer ones.

11
00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:48.566
Often the child reads a word with a silent e as if the e was not there.

12
00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:53.991
And words with two vowels together, like rain and boat, bring everything to a stop.

13
00:00:54.441 --> 00:01:00.165
It is a normal step. Until now, your child read one letter at a time, from left to right.

14
00:01:00.615 --> 00:01:05.898
A silent e breaks that rule. It sits at the end, and it changes a sound in the middle.

15
00:01:06.698 --> 00:01:11.203
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

16
00:01:11.653 --> 00:01:16.797
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

17
00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:22.504
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

18
00:01:22.954 --> 00:01:26.828
And there is one move for your child. Look at the end of the word first.

19
00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:30.918
Days two, three and four teach silent e, one vowel a day.

20
00:01:31.368 --> 00:01:35.485
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

21
00:01:35.935 --> 00:01:39.877
On day six the words are mixed. Some have the e, and some do not.

22
00:01:40.327 --> 00:01:42.647
Then come three pairs of vowels, one a day.

23
00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:45.864
Each pair is two letters that make one long sound.

24
00:01:50.096 --> 00:01:54.206
This plan teaches these three pairs only. The other pairs come after it.

25
00:01:55.006 --> 00:01:58.031
Now, what to expect. One small step at a time.

26
00:01:58.481 --> 00:02:03.314
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

27
00:02:03.764 --> 00:02:06.484
On day ten, the check gives you a clear next step.

28
00:02:07.284 --> 00:02:12.820
When your child misses the silent e, do not say the word. Say the same words, every time.

29
00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.803
Look at the end. Is there an e? Then wait.

30
00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:23.190
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

31
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:28.208
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

32
00:02:28.658 --> 00:02:31.806
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

33
00:02:32.256 --> 00:02:36.574
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

34
00:02:37.024 --> 00:02:41.801
On four of the days your child has a track to listen to. You press play and step away.

35
00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:47.018
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the card.

36
00:02:47.468 --> 00:02:52.557
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
